# Punctuation: hyphens and commas only

Never use em dashes (`—`, U+2014) or en dashes (`–`, U+2013). Use only the ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`, U+002D) and commas.

This applies to user-facing copy, docs, comments, commit messages, and agent output for this repo.

## Replacements

| Instead of | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Em dash for a break or aside | Comma, or split into two sentences |
| En dash in a numeric range | ASCII hyphen: `1-2`, `15-150` |
| Em dash as empty or missing value | ASCII hyphen `-`, or plain words such as `None` or `Not set` |
| En dash in compound modifiers | ASCII hyphen: `60-70%` |

## Examples

```
❌ Motion confirms interaction — it never decorates.
✅ Motion confirms interaction, it never decorates.

❌ Replace breakfast — why are you replacing it?
✅ Replace breakfast, why are you replacing it?

❌ 1–2 sessions per week
✅ 1-2 sessions per week

❌ {value ?? "—"}
✅ {value ?? "-"}
```

## Allowed

- ASCII `-` in compound words, kebab-case identifiers, minus signs, and numeric ranges
- Commas for lists, clauses, and pauses that would otherwise take an em dash

## Not allowed

- Pasting or typing `—` or `–`, including from smart punctuation or word processors
- Unicode dash entities in HTML or email copy (`&mdash;`, `&ndash;`)
